  ('zcrm_1579374000089145018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011740100', 'Rossana Johnston', NULL, '3-18-22 Requesting new Planstin cards. I responded via email.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-18 17:46:56', '2022-03-18 17:46:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089140023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078939522', 'Adrienne Mitra', NULL, '3-18-2022:  Adrienne called totally confused!  She says the gal that did her ''Welcome Call'' talked so fast she had a hard time comprehending what was being said.  (I can tell she needs a slower conversation.)  Then, the post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail didn''t arrive right away, so when she received it things weren''t very fresh for her.
     - We walked thru a good portion of the post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail.  I helped her w/basic understandings & let her know calling the concierge line is the perfect way to get guidance.
     - She mentioned her son is a gymnast (HS level, so not prof).
     - Went over extremely briefly Planstin prev has network & card, CirrusMD, Zion (& needs, alt  care requires pre-app) and submitting needs, no card, MAP*, etc.
     - She says she called the EAP Prog (MAP) and they gave her 2 counselors in her area.  She tried calling both:  1) Never answered & no machine  2) She was able to LM, but never heard back.  I encouraged her to call the MPA Assistance ph # again (& made sure she has the #) to let them know.  She asked what she does since there are only 2 providers.  I sugg she might be able to expand to the full state of AZ and do a virtual appt?
     - By the time we got off the phone I think she felt much better.  However, I expect we will talk to her again.  I gave her basics on ''cash-pay'', 1k IUA, & how to present if something happens.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-18 17:30:45', '2022-03-18 17:30:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089140018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080099002', 'Michelle Stevens', NULL, '3-18-2022:  John Kach let me know thier HCBB is now working.  Sent Michelle (&amp; Rick) the link and instructions (see e-mail below).  They sb all set!     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-18 14:55:55', '2022-03-18 14:55:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089145013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078546002', 'Alix Tingle', NULL, '3-18-22 From Me, "Hi Alix,

We could move you to a slightly different membership.  By doing so, you could then choose a higher IUA of $2500 with a $185 monthly fee. This brings your monthly fee down from $230 to $185 but increases your IUA from $500 to $2500 per incident.  So, if something bad happens you will have to pay much more if/when that happens with the $2500 IUA. We also need to make sure you don''t have any open Needs or health issues from the past 24 months to make a switch.

Let me know your thoughts.

Thanks"


Ok, thank you for this info Wendy!

I think i''ll keep my plan with the lower IUA of $500.

Thank you,
Alix', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-18 14:53:13', '2022-03-18 14:53:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089112098', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088571001', 'Roxanna Chavez', NULL, 'We finally got Employers Payment information for this employee.  Will input to admin 123.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-03-18 14:01:14', '2022-03-18 14:01:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089145008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089144002', 'Sarita Yeldandi', NULL, '3-18-22 Sarita enrolled into SECURE EF $1000/$715. She also enrolled in HMA $10000 for $155 because added to k ids. So, extra $5 for first kid and $10 for 2nd kid, up from $140. She might want to move her membership up or down in the future. If/when she builds up HMA enough, she''s thinking of moving IUA up and just using HMA to cover higher IUA. She''s all set and slightly nervous moving into the unknown away from Kaiser. She liked to see the Testimonial from the former Kaiser member as well!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-18 13:46:28', '2022-03-18 13:46:28'),
