  ('zcrm_1579374000088576036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044904504', 'Mariah Bauer', NULL, '3-11-22 Left vm for Mariah since she left me a vm today.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-11 17:51:14', '2022-03-11 17:51:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000088583008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086946002', 'William Alemaghides', NULL, '3-11-2022:  William is at the Urg Care Cntr & wasn''t sure what he tells them.  He had his Planstin card w/him - I let him know that will only be prev care & he will not use that at all today.  He understands he is a ''cash-pay'' pt today to his $2500 IUA.  To keep det inv & pymt receipts in case we need to start a need.
     - He was also fine w/me resending him a new link to sched his ''Welcome Call''.  He seems clueless as to why we asked him to resched.  Prob good if we can explain that when he has his call.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-11 17:31:26', '2022-03-11 17:31:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000088576031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060670268', 'Andrew Braudis', NULL, '3-11-22 Rachel is working for  a new company with super affordable benefits now but has an Open Need. ''m not 100% sure about what needs to happen with an Open Need prior to cancelling. I believe Zion requires them to be active while they are completing a Need. Rachel is going to call Zion on Monday about the status of the open Need. She''s submitted everything to them already. I asked her to ask them that question as well and let me know their answer. She also had her son''s annual wellness visit completed recently and she will call them on Monday to make sure they bill it to Planstin and coded it all as wellness. She''ll inquire about status of that bill too.  She''s had "the most pleasant "health insurance" patient-forward experience she''s ever had!" She''s super appreciative of the help she received from everyone throughout the process.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-11 17:26:09', '2022-03-11 17:26:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000088576026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000019634002', 'Colleen Mangeot', NULL, '3-11-22 She has an odd email from her Cobra benefits indicating she has to show proof of new ins plan without pre-x limitations. I don''t believe they can force her to continue paying for Cobra for 18 months, no matter what plan or no plan at all that she chooses. She''s going to call them on Monday for further clarification. She wants to enroll for May 1st ideally and not April 1st. But, she will join April 1st if need be and just be uncovered for the rest of March. She''ll let me know.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-11 17:05:59', '2022-03-11 17:05:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000088583003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082515013', 'Jennifer Mccray Rincon', NULL, '3-11-2022:  Jennifer called, she''s feeling very sick (thought she had food poisoning yesterday), but has realized she may need to see someone.  
     - We tried to get her into CirrusMD, but the invites (we tried multiple times & she''s been trying throughout the day  prior to calling) keep telling her the ''invitation has expired'' even though she just received it.  I submitted a support ticket for her to CirrusMD.
     - She says she''s never received ID cards for anything.  I sub a req to Planstin to resend her pdf & hardcopy cards to her (listed e-mail is accurate).
     - I also asked Kelly F to send her a new ''Welcome Pkt'' & went over the MPB.Health care w/her.
     - Sent her the temp for sched a ''Welcome Call'' as well.
     - She knows to keep her detailed inv & receipts if she ends up going to Urgent Care, the Dr, etc. & she''ll call to get instructions.  She knows she is ''cash-pay'' to her $2500 IUA.  [She wasn''t feeling well at all, so it was a super quick overview!]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-11 16:50:33', '2022-03-11 16:50:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000088576016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011716785', 'Megan Friday', NULL, '3-11-22 Megan called to get help/insurance for her daughter''s wisdom teeth that need to be pulled. I sent her Core Network and Core Choice with Spirit Dental to choose from. They don''t have a dentist/oral surgeon yet, so she''s going to find one in the network to get Core Network for $35.84 a month. Then the HMA can help them later for all other dental, medical, etc. They are using Life Care and found Jamie Gandolph who is  able to prescribe psychiatric meds. Her daughter is in the 2 month waiting period now. They are very happy with her! They were only given 3 names of local people and the other 2 were not viable. She let Mazetti and Sullivan know to update their list and they were super nice and helpful. Their son is in college now and qualifies for Medicaid and daughter may be able to get on great union plan soon. So, they may remove kids in the near future to lower their cost. Also their daughter just  fell into the orchestra pit when on stage that she didn''t know was there! She went to urgent care and got x-rays. May have broken a finger, got whiplash and there''s no treatment for that and perhaps some other small thing. She contemplating bringing cost to school since it was negligent on their part, but she''s not sure. They have a $2500 IUA and likely won''t reach it. But, I recommended she create the Need just in case it may exceed $2500 and she appreciated that suggestion and will work on it. Super thankful for my help and suggestions.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-11 15:37:11', '2022-03-11 15:37:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000088576008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088571001', 'Roxanna Chavez', NULL, '3-11-22 Rozanna is part of Daniel Siegrist''s employer group. She''s the 2nd employee and he''s the 1st. One more needed for List Bill. She chose List Bill on the app for Patti to pull the billing information to bill automatically monthly. Dan will pay entire membership fee for DIRECT with MPB and for Peak Med DPC on her behalf. His MPB cost is $270/$1000. She''s 36 and health, no concern for pre-x. She may add kids at a later date.  She also watched the video and I answered all of her questions and she successfully enrolled with Dan and I on the phone. April 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-11 15:01:21', '2022-03-11 15:01:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000088519008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082742002', 'Kara Baas', NULL, 'Welcome Call completed! ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-03-11 15:01:20', '2022-03-11 15:01:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000088576003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044781197', 'Daniel Siegrist', NULL, '3-11-22 Just enrolled Roxanna Chavez in Dan''s group. His company is paying for her entire membership with Peak Med and DIRECT $270/$1000 starting April 1st. He understands her membership is slightly different with Zion instead of Sedera for the MCS part and the rest the same.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-11 14:57:18', '2022-03-11 14:57:18'),
