  ('zcrm_1579374000088214008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000085054002', 'PAUL Finkelstein', NULL, '3-7-2022:  tt Paul.  He went for his prev annual appt & wondered about his labwork.  He called after-the-fact, so we realied his doc is not in network.  However, I spoke to Brian @ Planstin ~1:33pm:  Labwork does NOT have to be ordered by an in network doc to be covered.  Paul is going to have Quest or LabCorp do the labwork so it is in network.  He knows any uncovered items will kickback as uncovered, but sb at a network discounted price.  He may ask for pricing when he goes, just in case.   We did discuss his Planstin card is purely preventative care & the only time he will use that card.
     - He had me resend him the invite to sched a ''Welcome Call''.  He''ll try to find a time both he & Sara can attend.  I let him know this call is a good starting point for understanding his plan.
     - His MPB.Health cards: he wanted to know what they are for & we discussed the QRCode on the back.  He''ll try to get those setup as well.
     - IF he has something that isn''t prev, he may call to understand how to handle.  We discussed ''cash-pay'' pt to the $2500 IUA, but to call w/in first 4 mos in case we need to have him start a ''Need'', which has limited deadline for expenses to be considered.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-07 14:39:41', '2022-03-07 14:39:41'),
