  ('zcrm_1579374000086505013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763142', 'Leanne Wagner', NULL, 'Leanne called inquiring about her Dental and Vision benefits that are included with her plan. I advised Leanne that our plans currently do not cover dental, and vision and she seemed confused. She knew what she had to do on her end for dental and vision, she was calling and presenting herself as self-pay. Leanne understood that we currently do not offer dental or vision with any of our plans. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-02-14 09:26:05', '2022-02-14 09:26:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000086505008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005676955', 'Hillary Harris', NULL, 'I left Hillary a message pertaining to an email she sent Kelly (We believe it was intended for Kelly Anne). It appears that Diane is telling her members that the concierge team is able to take care of billing situations for the member. I have called Diane and left her a message stating that the concierge team is limited in what they can do when it comes to our members. We are unable to speak with any entity regarding billing with a member due to not being HIPAA certified. I have also reached out to the member via voicemail and email to let her know to contact me so that I can go over this situation with her. I have included Hillary''s email below:
On Sat, Feb 12, 2022, 8:59 PM Hillary Harris ~ SOUL PURPOSE <hillary@hillaryharris.com> wrote:
Hi Kelly -

Yesterday I got a notice from Planstin about what I think are lab tests from my OB/BYN LAST YEAR! First, I thought bloodwork was included in an annual exam. But in any case,
The notice provided the full amount and then an amount I am responsible for but also said that document was not a bill. It also said I have a deductible of $3000k but I thought my deductible was $1000 per incident and what does that have to do with lab work for what should be a covered regular annual exam?

Then today I got the bill from the lab but it was for the full amount and not the amount on the Planstin notice.

I am confused and frankly upset - I am still not understanding how this coverage works. I do not understand the fact that I am only get this notice over a year later. That the notice doesn’t match the lab bill. The deductible discrepancy. Or what I am supposed to do next. Do I contact Planstin? Do I contact the lab? This is exhausting to figure out.

Please e-mail me with a good time to go over this issue. I can also send you copies of the two documents if that will help. 
Thank you!
Prosperous Blessings,
~ Hillary Harris

~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-02-14 09:17:09', '2022-02-14 09:17:09'),
