  ('zcrm_1579374000084583098', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073820044', 'Kathryn Schneider', NULL, 'Kathryn called in and she had a few questions about how to use her services. She has a wellness visit scheduled for March and wanted to know how everything works. I told her about the provider having to be in the PHCS Network and then she would need to provide the provider with her Planstin card. Which she said she does not have, she only has her Zion & MPB.Health card. I gave her Planstin''s phone number to call them and order a new one. She also asked if a Women''s Well Visit is covered as well and I said yes, same process with the provider being in the network and handing her Planstin card. While I was on the phone I looked up both her regular wellness visit provider and her Gynecologist and both were in the network so she is good to go with that. Kathryn then asked if blood work for the physical is covered and I said yes as long as the facility she goes to is in the network as well and that ANY and ALL Quest Diagnostics and LabCorp are all covered and in the PHCS Network. She said that is perfect because they usually send her to Quest. So Kathryn is all set with all of her preventative appointments. She then asked about a surgery that she will be needing and asked about that process. I explained about Zion''s process and that there is no network but we have a service that we can look up specific procedures and find Fair Pricing in her area but she doesn''t HAVE to use them and can go anywhere of her choosing. She is responsible for her IUA of $1000 and anything there after Zion will cover after she submits her bills and starts a Need with them. I sent her the email explaining how to do that with Zion along with how to look up providers in the PHCS network for future times. She is all set and understands everything very well. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2022-01-14 10:31:04', '2022-01-14 10:31:04'),
