  ('zcrm_1579374000084428085', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082614002', 'AMY TANTAU', NULL, 'Amy called.  Now that she''s paid her membership fee believes we do everything for her.  She wanted me to find her a doctor so she could find a PCP and get her annual ck up,  etc.  She''s on Care+ = no prev &amp; she''s sure she''s supposed to have preventative!  I advised her to ck to call Leslie Jablonski (maybe she''s accidentally on the wrong plan?)    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-01-11 14:20:14', '2022-01-11 16:52:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000084454003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028419146', 'Reed Olson', NULL, 'List called in and had a bunch of questions and issues. She asked to speak to someone by the name of Sherri Richardson and I let her know that no one by that name works here. Lisa said she spoke to someone about a provider, etc. Figured out it was someone at RCI. She needed to get some questions answered about a bill that they are supposed to be helping her with and a few other things. I was able to give her RCI''s phone number. She then asked what we are for so I explained who we are and the reasons she would need to call into the Concierge. So that led to her having a bunch of other questions and she did not realize things about having to contact Sedera about "Needs" and anything about that. This is their first time needing to use the plan in that aspect & they have been members since 2019, so it makes sense she didn''t know or forgot. She has quite a few issues that need to be resolved now through Sedera. 1. Her husbands colonoscopy which first off should have been preventative but turns out polyps were found and the provider also had to do something else involving hemorrhoids I believe she said. So that automatically turns it into Diagnostic and not Preventative. She then said that they are only supposed to pay $1000 out of pocket for things like that and nothing more and I let her know that yes. Never anything more than their IUA of $1000 for Diagnostic. As long as they submit a Need with Sedera and proof of payment for the IUA. She had no idea she is supposed to do any of that with Sedera. Again it is their first time in years. So I emailed her the instructions on how to submit bills and open a Need with Sedera along with Sedera''s contact info to call. She also said that she went and had her regular eye exam and they found a growth. I told her same thing that she ONLY pays her IUA of $1000 and nothing more. If there is more than that amount to be paid she pays the $1000 out of pocket and asks to be billed the rest. Gets the receipts and bills and submits them to Sedera to start the process of a Need. Sedera with cover the rest of the costs after their IUA is paid in full. Lisa also needs a new RCI card to show when she goes for her mammogram and yearly wellness visit. Which she had me look up her provider for the physical and the provider IS in the PHCS network so she is good to go on that. Lisa then asked if a Flu shot is covered as preventative and I was not sure but I would be sending her the list of the 64+ ACA list of preventative items that are fully covered by RCI that she can check. If it is covered she can just send her bill/receipt to RCI and they will reimburse her. Lisa has quite a few things going on but they are all fairly simple and can be resolved quickly. I also let Lisa know about our new plans that we have to offer with Zion & Planstin due to the fact that they are cheaper and Sedera will be raising their prices soon. She was very very interested and happy to hear about this and will be contacting Andrea Hinman, her and her husbands Advisor that signed them on in 2019 and they will be switching. AFTER they get everything fixed and finished/straightened out with RCI and Sedera. I told her they can''t have any Open Needs with Sedera otherwise they will be considered Pre-existing. Other than all of that, I sent all emails she needed info on and was very very grateful for my time and helped her tremendously. Lastly I suggested a Welcome Call to go over everything with someone so they have a better and more clearer understanding of how the plan works and who is who doing what. All set. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2022-01-11 14:09:21', '2022-01-11 14:09:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000084428077', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442111', 'Sarah Getzelman', NULL, 'tt Sarah.  She was in panic mode because of confusion, but she''s actually sitting pretty.  
  - She submitted the ''need'' regarding Brian''s should surgery.  He did have the dr recently order a cat scan & surgery & they knew there was no sharing until the entered their 2nd yr w/Zion.  She''s aware the sharing amt is up to 25K now.  They are using Univ of UT Healthcare System.
  - Charles at Care Connect has contacted her & is working on the negotiation for a decreased rate.  She said she''s hearing 41k for the orig pricing + cat scan (but they offer 30% disc for cash-pay if nothing else = $28700).  So is aware they may still have some out-of-pocket.  
  - I went over the cards:  Planstin = Prev only & MUST always present for the preventative appts.  
  - Her hard copy Zion card:  no need to present the card (you are a cash-pay pt) until you have a submitted ''need'' where you''ve paid the $1000 IUA.  Then, past that you can present the card when you arrive for appts so the office can call for payment at time of service.  OR, you can continue submitting the detailed (& coded) invoices and any proof-of-pymts if you prefer.  She seemed to feel much better by the time we got off the phone.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-01-11 13:52:51', '2022-01-11 16:00:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000084428072', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005806201', 'Marti Winkler', NULL, 'Marti was chatting w/Julia, so I called &amp; walked Marti through Patti''s pymt chg form and e-mailed it to her conf e-mail address.  She used her corp cc so the fees are fine, but she knows if that chgs to go to an EFT for no feels.  She''ll get the form submitted.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-01-11 13:46:06', '2022-01-11 13:46:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000084428067', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048228219', 'Phil Saalborn', NULL, 'Phil called confused about why he had a pymt come thru from us.  It was only $25.75 so we went over that with the chg he had a $25 annual fee for the new comp.  I sent him a pymt chg temp form so he doesn''t have cc fees.  He wondered why his old EFT info wasn''t just pulled to the new pymt &amp; I explained that to him as well.  He''ll get the form sent right away.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-01-11 13:30:58', '2022-01-11 13:30:58'),
