  ('zcrm_1579374000084069013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082496002', 'Ryan Murphy', NULL, 'Raquel wants to know rate she signed up for.  We took care of a lot!
  - Sent her Patti''s plan change for so they can add her unique e-mail address to all the accounts.  It was just showing Ryan''s e-mail & he doesn''t get any of the business taken care of on the accounts.  raquel_jumonville@yahoo.com
  - She''s going to ask Patti for the e-mail regarding sending proof of self-employment on the Secure Plan so she can get Ryan to get this done .  The orig went to Ryan & he just won''t see it.   Since I can''t access Admin123 yet, she''ll tt Patti regarding this when they talk about the other changes she''s needing.  Sent Patti a Teams Chat so she know Raquel is needing this.
  - Her orig question about rate, I think was coming because their orig draw was elevated due to being on a cc.  She hadn''t realized there was a fee.  Sent her Patti''s pymt chg temp & she will get their EFT info submitted so the next draw is the reg amt.
  - Also sent her the orig e-mail with the ''Welcome Call'' link so she can get that scheduled.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-01-06 12:36:52', '2022-01-06 12:36:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000084069008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005806201', 'Marti Winkler', NULL, 'Marti called.  Fred needs to have kidney stone surgery & they want to go thru Care Connect.  Sent details* via e-mail to Jennifer since I don''t have access yet. Let Marti now she wouldn''t hear from until at least tomorrow maybe even next week if they need more info (I didn''t tell Marti this, but w/Jennifer out today, I know we can''t submit it until tomorrow).    

*Info (for future ref):
Patient = Fred Winkler
Contact = wife:  Marti Winkler  530-620-8135  martiwinkler147@gmail.com (=confirmed both)
Urologist:  Marshall Health in Plasterville, CA    Dr. Jason Nelles  530-676-6131', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-01-06 12:18:38', '2022-01-06 12:18:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000084066008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000013590075', 'Jason Adams', NULL, '1-6-21 Jason is wanting to convert to DIRECT. He and wife are still members of Nextera. No pre-x other than a toe issue with wife, I believe. They can pay $455 a month Feb. 1st moving forward and keep their Sept. 2020 start date with Zion. They are past the initial year of pre-x benefit already. So, no impact by switching moving forward. We will complete the new enrollment for DIRECT and cancellation process for MPB CareZ Worksite Bridge this afternoon.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-01-06 12:16:34', '2022-01-06 12:16:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000084069003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080945002', 'Macay Hunter', NULL, 'tt Joan.  I did direct Macay properly.  It does sound like he is on the wrong plan and that the coverages he was told would start in 6 months are not even a part of his plan!  
  - tt Patti & Joan.  Joan is going to call Wendy to work on helping the advisor know this plan doesn''t have the immunizations & that he must re-enroll the member on the proper Secure Plan (Macay is self-employed) for a 2/1/22 start date.
  - I called Macay & LM.  Let him know he should hear from Jeff Kanter by beg of next week & to call me if he hasn''t.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-01-06 12:06:13', '2022-01-06 12:06:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000084066003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000051949076', 'Michelle Smith', NULL, '1-6-22 Apparently she''s getting billed at $280 bc of an error on MPB side. I don''t see this showing anywhere. At $280/$500 IUA then CARE+ and SECURE make more sense for her even at $1000 IUA. She''s engaged to be married this summer or fall. She''s 35 and fiance 47. She doesn''t have any health issues and is a yoga teacher. She has an HSA but hasn''t been funding it or using it. She''s considering CARE+ or SECURE. She did her pap in April 2017, again in 2020 and up for the next one in 2023. If funds HSA then worth SECURE or if has baby in the future then SECURE is best. She knows of the 2 month wait and that''s no issue. She also pays $119 to Modern Dentistry for 3 cleanings a year and discounts on more services. Told her that''s a great deal and possibly use HSA or HMA for any other costs. The HMA is fantastic way to plan for cost around maternity and $1000 IUA. She wants to learn. She knows of the 20th of the month deadline for the conversion and to lock in price through Oct. 2022. Also knows cost to add baby and soon to be husband if/when those happen in the future. Not pregnant, just planning.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-01-06 12:00:18', '2022-01-12 13:12:04'),
