  ('zcrm_1579374000083677008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000083475001', 'John Hunt', NULL, '1-3-22 Patti is refunding the $100 that I forgot to waive since he''s an ASHI member. He has chronic kidney disease which is stable. He sees a Dr. 2x a year for blood work and urine analysis. I made the pre-x clause extremely clear many times as I was hesitant for him to join. He and his wife discussed it and they chose to move forward. I expressed my concerns to both of them just in case there was any confusion. They feel confident in their decision. His wife is healthy, John is 51 and wife is 50. They are tired of traditional insurance with the crazy high ded and mop. However, they were only paying $100 he says but he doesn''t want to have to worry about how much income he makes and such.  They are excited to try this for a year at least. They watched the video before they called me. They do not use tobacco, wife no health issues. He does take some generic meds which we looked up and none were expensive. We also looked up Dr. Roger Guillemette at BJC Medical Group of Missouri. I found this group accepts the PHCS PPO / Multiplan. Still told him to double check before they go. They wanted a Jan. 1st start date which Patti honored. They enrolled on the 30th of Dec., 2021.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-01-03 11:58:57', '2022-01-03 11:58:57'),
