  ('zcrm_1579374000083062024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021695264', 'Lorie Moreno-Roch', NULL, '12-27-21 Anthem Gold Pathway X HMO 1400 Rx Copay Gold HMO $3,055.97, $0 APTC. Submitted on 12/16/21.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-12-27 15:51:55', '2021-12-27 15:51:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000083062016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021695264', 'Lorie Moreno-Roch', NULL, '12-15-21 ﻿
Hi Lorie,

It looks like you will want to stick with Anthem to keep UC Health. It then means you will have to find other doctors for everything else you mentioned. The Anthem Silver Plan you have now should suffice. I included two other options to review. It honestly will just depends on what truly happens throughout the year as to what might be better. The Gold Plan has the most co-pays but then anything beyond the office visit will be billed anyhow. The insurance companies have the math figured out. It''s hard to win this game. None of these plans will remove you from paying a bunch of bills unless you purely have doctor visits and no labs, testing or anything else associated with the visit.

Take a look!

Cheers,

Wendy

Was with Sedera and cancelled for Jan. 2020. Didn''t select me as agent for 2020. But, now back to being their agent for 2022 with reg ins.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-12-27 15:43:46', '2021-12-27 15:49:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000083044166', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077918048', 'Bryan Schiff', NULL, 'Bryan called regarding prescriptions. I explained the prescription quote process and sent Bryan a prescription quote form via email. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-12-27 14:53:14', '2021-12-27 14:53:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000083062008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028171532', 'Christine Torres', NULL, '12-27-21 I talked with Christine and she wants more extensive coverage which she feels she needs as she gets older. She''s been with Kaiser forever and is choosing to go back to Kaiser for more money and in her view more benefits with co-pays and such.  She just feels more comfortable with it and wants a prescription drug program and such. It''s not about price more about her comfort of utilization.  She actually never even used her PSDHC. But, it was clear she had already made up her mind. She was appreciative of my willingness to help.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-12-27 14:45:50', '2021-12-27 14:54:57'),
