  ('zcrm_1579374000080847050', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000054986001', 'Ken Trombley', NULL, '11-29-21 I just auto renewed his Kaiser medical and Anthem Dental. " You will be given a tax credit of $478.79/month. Your cost will be $222.33/mo. You can let it auto renew or I can just push it through to be certain. Do you want to keep your dental insurance as well for $9.85 a month?" Complete for 2022 on both products.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-11-29 18:26:50', '2021-11-29 18:26:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000080847045', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082489061', 'Emily Meneghel', NULL, '11-29-21 Emily is 41, husband 45 and two boys, 6 and 9. They currently have health insurance through her husbands employer but he leaving that and going to be real estate agent. They were quoted $1200 month for Humana $11K ded and $13,100 MOP. They are healthy. Only health issue was Emily had a hysterectomy in Sept. 2020. Now she just takes hormone replacements and typical women''s well check. Takes estradial patch and generic is fine, plus premarin cream which Anthem or Cigna is charging them $900 for. She doesn''t have to have it though. She loves the sound of this. SECURE $1000/$685. She said it makes so much more sense.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-11-29 16:28:17', '2021-11-29 16:28:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000080847037', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000689078', 'Kim Gangwish Zahorik', NULL, '11-29-21Renewed  Cigna Connect HSA Bronze 6500 for $606.59, APTC $316.52. Jake got covid recently and it put him down for 12 days. They use a Functional Dr. in FC and he helped him with various supplements. That Dr. says IVM doesn''t work for Delta variant. I''ve never heard that. Anyhow, all set for 2022!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-11-29 15:43:05', '2021-11-29 15:55:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000080847026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041906167', 'Pamela Tuck', NULL, '11-29-21 Court was planning to cancel membership and go without insurance and just keep Nextera. But once I told him I can bring the cost back down he was thrilled. He didn''t want regular insurance at all since past experience was so bad. It cost $12K for the year and they covered nothing. So, choosing DIRECT with Nextera for $455 for ES/$1000.  Due to his age he was paying $700+ to Sedera and Nextera''s fee which isn''t sustainable now that he''s retired. Enrolled now and will walk him through cancellation process next.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-11-29 15:27:58', '2021-11-29 15:30:07'),
