  ('zcrm_1579374000077289011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067333056', 'Joe Werne', NULL, '10-11-21 Chose Kaiser again for Oct. 1st start date with income estimated at about $30K. Lost employer coverage.  Also has Delta Dental which I need to check on commissions soon.

10-11-21 hi wendy:

last friday i seemed to be in a game of phone hot-potato (is that a thing?) as kaiser told me to call “connect for health co,” and vice versa, so eventually kaiser patched C4HCO into a 3-way phone call, and i was told to call next week to make sure the paperwork got through, and then i could pay my premium to make sure i was covered (which they assured me i was).

today’s update: 

1. i called kaiser today, and they verified i had a policy in place, and i paid the premium.

2. after delta told me it might take 30 days (really?) to get into their system, i called C4HCO and discovered they’d never sent the paperwork over to C4HCO, so they did that (finally) today. i was instructed to try again with Delta next week.

thanks for your help with this.

-joe', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-10-11 11:56:09', '2021-10-11 11:57:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000077231016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014743027', 'Jay Land', NULL, 'Jay called.  His banking acct was compromised.  Sent him Patti''s template for payment chg of info.  He''s going to complete it and send it right away.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-10-11 11:48:09', '2021-10-11 11:48:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000077289003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079737009', 'Kari Riley', NULL, '10-11-21 Kari is 54 and kids 17 and 21 (daughter). Kari''s husband passed away recently within the past year or two. She has enough money to live on and currently has $40K income as Survivor''s Benefit. She Might have mild, chronic pancreatitis and will know within next few days after CT scan. It could be a problem in 15-20 years from now. But, they don''t know how to treat it now other than with great diet and exercise which she is focusing. It could simply be due to stress of past two years. She also takes Premarin cream for hormones/estogen. She uses 4 tubes per year, as needed. Sometimes uses it 2x per week at 1 gram. She can also replace it with Estradiol cream in tube at same amount. Daughter takes birth control and nothing else for rest of them. Kari will need a colonoscopy within another year or so. She wants SECURE if possible and is willing to start her old business of selling art again and getting business license to do so. If not, she''s fine paying cash for small stuff but not ideal for colonoscopy. Her income qualifies her for APTC as well and she may choose that instead bc of pre-x. We will explore in early Nov. with our meeting set already. She''s in no rush and just wants a Jan. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-10-11 11:46:05', '2021-10-11 11:50:44'),
